  "no alias analysis: q = P; q[\"days\"] is published as a different receiver even though both names may hold one dict -- each row carries both receiver texts so the 34-line population can be checked by eye",
  "a mutation of the object is not a rebinding of the name: m[\"k\"] read twice with m[\"k\"] = ... in between still counts as the same object, which is what object identity means but not what value identity would mean",
  "in-place aliasing through a function argument (f(m) mutating m) is invisible",
  "the receiver has to be a nameable chain; f()[\"k\"] and [a][b][\"k\"] are published as computed and are not decided either way",
