 "verdict": "4_of_6_superseded_duplicate_reads_read_the_same_object_as_the_dead_line",
 "answer": "E623 published 34 dead face-key lines in live holders and classed 6 as superseded duplicate reads -- a later read of the same literal key.  Under object identity 4 of those 6 read the same object as the dead line and 2 read a different one, so 2 lines lose that class and are re-published as another_object_is_read_instead.  Across all 34 lines there are 26 sibling reads: 19 are the same receiver bound once, 0 the same receiver rebound in between, 7 a different receiver expression, and 0 sit on a receiver that is a computed expression; corrected, 4 lines are superseded duplicates on the same object, 7 read the same object only before the dead line, 2 read another object instead, and 21 are the only read of that key on that object in the function"
}
